  "message": "I’d suggest building a single “assistant‑wrapper” agent that knows how to call the existing specialists (the web‑page generator, the spreadsheet creator, etc.). When you invoke it, it can check what parameters you’ve supplied, ask you for anything that’s missing (like the year or which category), store the answers, and then hand off to the right underlying agent.  \n\nThat way you only have one entry point to remember, and you keep the prompting logic in one place. If the tasks become very different in how they work or need separate security/permissions, you could still split them later, but a flexible wrapper gives you the interactive experience you want right now.",
